{
 "about": "Driftlog country stamps for the passport page (https://driftlog-counter.pages.dev/passport/). The landmark drawings, frame shapes and ink colours are the ones in the Driftlog iPhone app; the layout (English name in capitals, no date) is the one on the 194-stamp poster at https://driftlog-app.pages.dev/stamps/.",
 "definition": "194 = the 193 UN member states + Taiwan, the same set the counter counts. This set has no stamp for Vatican City, Kosovo, Palestine, Western Sahara or territories such as Hong Kong.",
 "count": 194,
 "image": {
  "format": "WebP, lossless, transparent (sRGB)",
  "sheets": [
   "stamps/sheet-0.webp",
   "stamps/sheet-1.webp",
   "stamps/sheet-2.webp",
   "stamps/sheet-3.webp"
  ],
  "sheetPx": 1680,
  "stampPx": 240,
  "cols": 7,
  "perSheet": 49,
  "order": "The table order of kit.js (ISO 3166-1 alpha-2, alphabetical): country i is on sheet floor(i/49), column (i%49)%7, row floor((i%49)/7). x and y below are the same position in pixels.",
  "canvasPt": 168,
  "stampPt": 160,
  "marginPt": 4,
  "stampRatio": 0.952381,
  "notes": [
   "Every page that uses the stamps loads all four sheets, whichever countries it shows, so the requests do not reveal a list of countries.",
   "The 160pt stamp frame is centred in a 168pt square cell, so the frame is stampRatio of the cell side.",
   "Rotation is not baked in. appRotateDeg is the tilt the app's passport screen uses (-8 to +8, positive = clockwise, the same sign as canvas ctx.rotate() and CSS rotate()); rotateDeg is the poster's (-3 to +3). Rotate about the cell centre; a square turned by t needs a box of side x (|cos t| + |sin t|), about 1.13x at 8 degrees.",
   "The faint fill inside the frame is the ink at 7% alpha, not an opaque colour, so it tints whatever it is drawn on. On the poster paper (#FAF6EF) it looks the same as the poster.",
   "bbox = measured extent of non-transparent pixels, as fractions of the cell side [x0, y0, x1, y1]."
  ]
 },
 "shapes": {
  "circle": {
   "w": 1.0,
   "h": 1.0,
   "note": "circle filling the frame"
  },
  "roundedRect": {
   "w": 1.0,
   "h": 1.0,
   "cornerRadius": 0.08125,
   "note": "continuous corners, radius 13pt"
  },
  "hexagon": {
   "w": 0.86603,
   "h": 1.0,
   "note": "pointy top and bottom; narrower than the frame"
  }
 },
